Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 06:39:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 062/119] scene-referred S0: review fixes - cached request
 pointer, in-place target reformat

Two follow-ups from the S0 review.

1. IsSceneReferred() no longer resolves the request by name on every call. It ran up to three
   times a frame (pipeline resource update plus two tone-map sites) and GetByName() is a CRC
   plus a map lookup behind a one-entry per-thread cache that the other post-effect params keep
   evicting. CPostEffectsMgr::GetSceneReferredParam() returns the m_pUserSceneReferred already
   resolved at Init(), so the hot path is a pointer read. Release() deletes the params through
   the name map and left every cached CEffectParam* dangling; ours is the one read from outside
   the class, so it is now nulled there. The comment at the read site records that the value is
   the one CParamFloat::SyncMainWithRender() copied into this thread's slot at the frame
   boundary - it is the request ccam made for this frame and cannot change under a frame in
   flight.

2. Dangling-pointer audit of the seven re-formatted targets, and the mechanism changed as a
   result. All 30 uses across RenderDll were classified (table now in
   scene-notes/research/s0-hdr-format-selection.md section 6, replacing the open question).
   Nobody caches a raw CTexture* - every site reads m_graphicsPipelineResources at use time.
   The hazard is one level down: the binding recorded in a resource set or device render pass,
   combined with the IsDirty() guards that decide whether a stage re-issues its Set* calls. Ten
   such (b) sites exist - CToneMappingStage's $HDRFinalBloom slot (key is sun-shafts / chart /
   luminance IDs), CBloomStage's m_pass2V.IsDirty() which takes no arguments at all, the streak
   and halation composites, CTiledShadingStage's UAV, CScreenSpaceSSS twice, and
   CScreenSpaceReflections. Releasing the objects would let the eResourceDestroyed callback NULL
   those bindings, and nothing would ever set them again.

   Fixing ten sites means editing eight engine stages, which is the opposite of what a
   byte-identity change should do. So the release was dropped entirely: the new
   CTexture::ReformatRenderTarget() sets the format and re-runs CreateDeviceTexture(), swapping
   the device texture underneath the same CTexture object. Every pointer stays valid, and
   SetDevTexture() raises eDeviceResourceDirty, which both CDeviceResourceSet and
   CDeviceRenderPass turn into "rebuild your views" rather than "your binding is gone". That is
   the sanctioned mechanism - it is what OwnDevTexture() exists for. (a), (b) and (c) all become
   moot, and UpdateHDRSatelliteFormats() no longer calls the create functions at all.

   Our own DOF / ghost / diffraction / FFT glare code holds none of the seven; the only contact
   is CBloomStage's halation and streak composites, which are in the table.

Built clean (0 errors, 0 warnings outside Code/SDKs): CryRenderD3D11, CinematicCamera.

